WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.970
All's well that ends well

00:05.080 --> 00:10.330
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

00:05.080 --> 00:10.330
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

00:08.030 --> 00:21.300
Junjou Romantica 2

00:10.330 --> 00:13.800
ima futari no story

00:10.330 --> 00:13.800
Now, our story...

00:15.090 --> 00:22.580
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

00:15.090 --> 00:22.580
Our future is going to shine on.

00:26.020 --> 00:31.310
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

00:26.020 --> 00:31.310
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

00:31.780 --> 00:36.140
okubyou ni naru bakari

00:31.780 --> 00:36.140
and always lose my nerve.

00:36.140 --> 00:41.740
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

00:36.140 --> 00:41.740
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

00:41.740 --> 00:45.370
kimi to aeru nara

00:41.740 --> 00:45.370
if it means I can see you.

00:47.400 --> 00:52.380
ame ni utarete furueru koe

00:47.400 --> 00:52.380
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

00:52.710 --> 00:57.980
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

00:52.710 --> 00:57.980
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

00:58.660 --> 01:01.460
boku wa yuku yo

00:58.660 --> 01:01.460
I'll go,

01:01.460 --> 01:08.210
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

01:01.460 --> 01:08.210
Until the day when I can see you.

01:09.030 --> 01:14.220
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:09.030 --> 01:14.220
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:14.220 --> 01:17.930
ima futari no story

01:14.220 --> 01:17.930
Now, our story

01:18.090 --> 01:19.740
ugokidashita

01:18.090 --> 01:19.740
has started.

01:19.740 --> 01:24.730
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

01:19.740 --> 01:24.730
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

01:24.730 --> 01:31.920
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

01:24.730 --> 01:31.920
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

01:40.320 --> 01:42.290
Thank you very much, Misaki-kun!

01:42.730 --> 01:45.700
All this was because Sensei forgot to bring his manuscript!

01:45.810 --> 01:48.370
You didn't have to run here till you were out of breath.

01:48.370 --> 01:50.180
It's your damn fault, isn't it!!?

01:50.620 --> 01:53.120
Misaki-kun, thanks a lot for today.

01:53.450 --> 01:56.460
There are some Kuma cream puffs in the editorial office on the 5th floor, so take them with you, okay?

01:56.770 --> 01:58.170
Oh, thank you!

01:58.530 --> 02:00.460
Come one Sensei, we should get going!

02:02.800 --> 02:05.610
Hmm, so this how a publishing company looks, huh?

02:07.290 --> 02:11.100
Now that I think about it, this is the first time I've seen an "office".

02:18.010 --> 02:19.570
Wh-What!?

02:21.920 --> 02:22.760
What?

02:22.930 --> 02:24.760
Oh, n-nothing!

02:25.080 --> 02:26.810
<i>That's what I'd like to ask!!</i>

02:28.740 --> 02:30.640
Wh-Wh-Wh-What's up with him?

02:30.890 --> 02:33.360
He looked like Usagi-san when he's in crunch time.

02:32.820 --> 02:37.800
Editorial office

02:40.000 --> 02:43.050
<i>I'll never work for a publishing company.</i>

02:45.760 --> 02:47.420
Hey! It's the little cutie!

02:47.570 --> 02:48.900
Oh, Isaka-san!

02:49.090 --> 02:50.080
What's up?

02:50.340 --> 02:54.010
Usagi-san forgot his manuscript for a meeting, so I just came to deliver it.

02:54.180 --> 02:56.080
Oh ho, thanks a lot.

02:56.250 --> 02:59.640
Oh yeah, if any books here catch your interest, you can have them.

02:59.800 --> 03:00.970
Oh no!

03:01.260 --> 03:03.010
You don't have to be so polite.

03:03.010 --> 03:05.280
Oh no, really...

03:05.810 --> 03:09.280
Box: Bizarre Chef The Kan. Premium deluxe version comes with "The Kan" figure!

03:06.090 --> 03:09.010
"The Kan!" That too a limited edition I never bought!

03:09.520 --> 03:11.650
Oh, do you like that manga?

03:12.820 --> 03:13.840
<i>What should I do?</i>

03:14.900 --> 03:17.200
<i>I'm ridiculously happy right now!</i>

03:17.770 --> 03:21.300
<i>I'm sorry about thinking that Isaka-san is hard to get along with.</i>

03:21.850 --> 03:23.960
<i>He looks like a God right now!</i>

03:26.300 --> 03:28.280
Sensei! Please calm down!!

03:28.280 --> 03:29.650
What's this? What happened?

03:30.050 --> 03:32.620
Oh, director! It's Ijuuin-sensei!

03:32.720 --> 03:33.880
Again!?

03:35.000 --> 03:38.880
Sensei, it's alright. Please keep drawing till you feel satisfied.

03:39.050 --> 03:41.520
I'll do something about the printers.

03:41.650 --> 03:45.490
It's a lie! No one's waiting for my manga!

03:45.880 --> 03:49.540
Oh yeah! Sensei, here! There's a huge fan of yours right here!

03:49.600 --> 03:50.260
Eh?

03:50.960 --> 03:53.820
Cutie, this person here is the author of "The Kan".

03:53.920 --> 03:54.480
Eh?

03:54.940 --> 03:56.960
It's Ijuuin Kyou-sensei!

04:05.320 --> 04:09.410
<i>This guy... wrote my bible!!!?</i>

04:09.850 --> 04:14.450
Hmph! That's just superficial! You'll just fall in love with some other authors work soon enough!

04:14.450 --> 04:15.900
That won't happen!

04:16.130 --> 04:19.380
I always look forward to your work!

04:19.600 --> 04:23.900
I could only buy your comics before, but I also buy magazines now!

04:24.090 --> 04:29.090
I've been reading "The Kan" since a long time! Half of my life is made up of you!

04:29.090 --> 04:31.620
I absolutely love Sensei!!

04:38.490 --> 04:41.740
E-Even if you say so...

04:44.000 --> 04:47.060
See, Sensei! You have some serious fans here!

04:47.060 --> 04:49.120
Just a little bit more! Let's work hard!

04:48.480 --> 04:51.700
Sensei! All the best! I'll be rooting for you!!

04:52.120 --> 04:54.100
It really was him! In the flesh!!

04:54.240 --> 04:56.720
You really were a big help there, cutie!

05:02.170 --> 05:03.840
U-Usagi-san?

05:04.770 --> 05:06.220
Eh? A-Ahh!!

05:10.100 --> 05:11.700
W-What's up?

05:11.700 --> 05:13.700
That should be my line.

05:13.900 --> 05:16.900
What are you thinking, shouting out a confession in a place like this?

05:17.090 --> 05:20.250
Confession? Oh, is this about Ijuuin-sensei?

05:20.600 --> 05:23.320
You know, he's the one who wrote a manga I love.

05:23.320 --> 05:24.940
Besides, Sensei's a guy.

05:25.040 --> 05:28.940
That's only more trouble! Going all sparkly eyed, are you stupid!?

05:28.940 --> 05:30.020
Hah?

05:30.090 --> 05:33.890
If you meet someone you admire, you'd obviously be excited, won't you?

05:34.050 --> 05:35.930
My heart's just so squeezy~!

05:36.040 --> 05:38.300
No, more like it's going all mushy~!

05:40.610 --> 05:43.460
Oh no! I should have requested his autograph!

05:43.570 --> 05:46.500
But, he seemed pretty busy, so I guess it wouldn't be possible.

05:47.930 --> 05:49.360
W-Wai- Usagi-!!

05:49.480 --> 05:52.360
Hiiii!!! Office mode love is forbidden!!

05:53.100 --> 05:55.400
You're mistaken!! What are you saying!!?

05:55.610 --> 05:57.400
Sensei, we've got to go!!

05:57.570 --> 05:59.770
It's already past our meeting time!

06:01.330 --> 06:02.980
Enough! I'm going home!

06:02.980 --> 06:03.660
Hey!

06:03.660 --> 06:04.810
Sensei!

06:05.090 --> 06:07.000
Hey, do your job!

06:07.930 --> 06:10.620
Director, Usami-sama has arrived.

06:22.900 --> 06:29.220
Oh yes, one of our books that's being adapted to a film will be distributed by his company.

06:29.400 --> 06:31.600
We're having a meeting regarding that today.

06:33.450 --> 06:34.610
Let's go, Misaki.

06:35.100 --> 06:36.720
Sensei, you have a meeting!

06:36.840 --> 06:39.130
I told you, do whatever you like!

06:39.370 --> 06:41.130
It's your work, isn't it?

06:41.130 --> 06:43.980
And you don't even have the capability of fulfilling the duties of your work?

06:46.080 --> 06:48.380
<i>Oh no! This atmosphere's bad!!</i>

06:48.380 --> 06:51.860
Alright, alright, alright! I'll head back immediately, so please get back to your work.

06:52.080 --> 06:55.960
Okay? Okay? It's okay. I won't make any detours on my way back and just head home.

06:56.250 --> 06:57.380
There, there!

06:57.620 --> 06:59.770
Make sure to call me when you reach home.

07:00.060 --> 07:03.130
Yes, yes! Understood! Bye then!

07:08.020 --> 07:09.800
Okay then, I'll excuse myself too-

07:09.800 --> 07:13.490
Cutie, I'll give you a chance to get Ijuuin-sensei's autograph.

07:16.300 --> 07:18.970
Please wait here with Haruhiko. I'll be right back.

07:19.050 --> 07:20.970
Hey, wait-! Isaka-san!!

07:21.260 --> 07:23.960
Don't shout. It'll only be a bother.

07:24.100 --> 07:25.340
But still!

07:25.620 --> 07:29.370
He said he'd be right back. How about you wait just a little?

07:30.090 --> 07:31.220
Yeah...

07:32.380 --> 07:36.320
<i>Actually, being here with Usagi's brother is more problematic.</i>

07:37.810 --> 07:41.010
In the end, it looks like you went to Atami with my father.

07:41.290 --> 07:41.900
What?

07:42.340 --> 07:47.100
You both had a bath together and talked about bears until you fainted in the water.

07:47.320 --> 07:51.570
That's not true! No, I mean, it's not false either, but it's not quite correct.

07:52.090 --> 07:53.180
It's not?

07:53.320 --> 07:58.100
I went there with Usagi-san. And coincidentally met your father.

08:00.010 --> 08:00.880
Is that so.

08:01.220 --> 08:01.970
Yes.

08:02.650 --> 08:07.570
E-Eh... Uh... A-And then, we went to Hamamatsu from Atami.

08:07.570 --> 08:10.010
And for some reason, we ended up buying some eels.

08:10.120 --> 08:11.530
That's the specialty there, after all.

08:11.570 --> 08:14.810
Oh, we didn't buy them to eat, but bought them as pets!

08:12.080 --> 08:15.500
To buy

08:13.800 --> 08:15.500
To keep as a pet

08:14.810 --> 08:17.020
Eels as pets, crazy, right?!

08:17.260 --> 08:22.850
On top of that, I have to take care of the marimo, plastic models, bears and what not.

08:23.560 --> 08:26.280
I see. That must be tough.

08:26.570 --> 08:27.180
<i>Huh?</i>

08:28.850 --> 08:31.890
<i>Huuuuh!!? Usagi's brother smiled?</i>

08:32.340 --> 08:34.180
<i>So a person like him can also smile, huh?</i>

08:35.890 --> 08:40.620
<i>Come to think of it, he seems much mellow than when I met him before.</i>

08:41.210 --> 08:44.330
Did my father saying something weird to you again?

08:44.780 --> 08:45.380
Huh?

08:46.360 --> 08:52.240
He does say things that he thinks are correct, but you don't have to worry about it.

08:52.720 --> 08:55.960
Oh no, he didn't really say anything to me.

08:56.320 --> 09:01.620
<i>Hm? Could it be, that he's worried about me?</i>

09:02.300 --> 09:06.420
The Usami group will be leading the construction of some large scale commercial facilities.

09:06.850 --> 09:09.730
I've decided to take full charge of the projects.

09:09.730 --> 09:11.730
Eh? Oh! I see.

09:12.080 --> 09:17.170
I may not be able to draw plans myself, but I can at least be involved in architecture.

09:17.210 --> 09:18.780
Oh! Then...!

09:19.760 --> 09:22.840
I actually wanted to be architect.

09:23.570 --> 09:25.050
Did you give up on it?

09:25.160 --> 09:28.290
Even though you can create beautiful buildings like the aquarium? That's too bad!

09:30.660 --> 09:32.050
It's all thanks to you.

09:32.050 --> 09:34.940
What? Oh, no no!! I didn't really do anything!

09:35.520 --> 09:38.080
I need you.

09:40.970 --> 09:43.890
Uh, that is, what are you saying?

09:44.020 --> 09:45.490
I love you.

09:46.490 --> 09:47.620
S-Sto-

09:49.020 --> 09:52.730
Your right choice would be to choose me.

09:52.730 --> 09:55.280
To begin with, I'm a guy, you know!

09:55.400 --> 09:57.280
I know that.

09:59.450 --> 10:00.570
What are you doing?

10:00.860 --> 10:04.160
Oh!  O-Oh, hey, Akihiko! What's this? So you ran away?

10:04.330 --> 10:06.740
I didn't. Our meeting's over.

10:06.920 --> 10:08.920
Oh, that sure was fast!

10:09.680 --> 10:11.330
Those are Misaki's, right?

10:11.780 --> 10:12.530
Where is he?

10:12.730 --> 10:14.530
Let's see, bathroom.

10:15.340 --> 10:16.720
And where is <i>he</i>?

10:16.960 --> 10:19.120
He's is the bathroom too, maybe.

10:19.500 --> 10:20.560
Don't.

10:22.500 --> 10:23.540
Step aside.

10:23.960 --> 10:26.760
Isn't this the perfect chance? Test him a little.

10:26.900 --> 10:30.170
See how he reacts when he's forced by another man.

10:30.320 --> 10:32.620
What are you thinking? This is no joke!

10:32.850 --> 10:38.100
To begin with, you understand, don't you, that if things aren't set straight, it's all going to become messy.

10:38.580 --> 10:40.100
It's none of your business!

10:40.940 --> 10:43.140
The one who will decide is cutie.

10:47.650 --> 10:48.690
I'm sorry.

10:53.100 --> 10:56.920
I-It's not that I hate you or anything.

10:57.250 --> 11:00.040
To begin with, I'm a guy. So...

11:00.260 --> 11:02.440
So it's a different story if it's Akihiko, huh.

11:02.440 --> 11:04.980
U-Uh, no, well...

11:05.700 --> 11:06.800
He's...

11:13.960 --> 11:14.890
<i>Not good.</i>

11:15.260 --> 11:17.360
<i>Haruhiko-san is serious about this.</i>

11:18.820 --> 11:21.880
What does Akihiko have that I don't?

11:23.420 --> 11:26.250
If I understand that, I can improve on it.

11:26.400 --> 11:30.700
No, in fact, Usagi-san might be the one lacking in things.

11:31.620 --> 11:33.460
He can't really do anything by himself.

11:33.560 --> 11:35.900
And if I just leave him be, he'll seriously just go off somewhere.

11:36.500 --> 11:40.320
It's just that, if I'm not watching him always, I just get very worried.

11:41.050 --> 11:42.210
Do you love him?

11:42.500 --> 11:45.530
Oh, no!! I-I mean, it's not something so simple!

11:45.610 --> 11:48.100
I mean, we are both men to begin with!

11:48.680 --> 11:50.340
So, I mean...

11:50.540 --> 11:53.940
Uh, what's this? What was I talking about again?

11:54.820 --> 11:57.420
Uh... So... that is...

11:59.620 --> 12:00.500
Yes.

12:01.780 --> 12:02.740
I'm sorry.

12:03.240 --> 12:06.050
I can't choose you, Haruhiko-san.

12:12.300 --> 12:14.740
Is what he says. Are you satisfied?

12:14.960 --> 12:15.490
Huh?

12:22.810 --> 12:26.450
Hey! What the hell!!!? Bastard! Stop listening on other people's conversation!!

12:26.640 --> 12:29.900
I was just passing by this room. You're the one who was blabbering.

12:30.050 --> 12:31.900
Don't shift the blame on me!!!

12:32.050 --> 12:36.490
Alright, alright, alright. Haruhiko it's time to get back to work.

12:38.650 --> 12:39.460
Um...

12:40.740 --> 12:42.660
All the best for your work.

12:43.360 --> 12:44.320
I mean it.

12:51.940 --> 12:54.220
H-Hey! What are you doing!?

12:54.220 --> 12:56.220
A physical examination of course.

12:56.330 --> 12:57.700
Let go!

12:56.330 --> 12:57.920
He didn't do anything to you, did he?

12:57.690 --> 13:00.220
Let go! I said, let go!!

12:58.920 --> 13:01.420
If you don't look at me properly, I'll go off somewhere.

13:01.690 --> 13:04.060
Don't threaten me like that!

13:04.520 --> 13:06.060
Then, I beg you.

13:06.850 --> 13:08.320
Stay by my side.

13:09.120 --> 13:11.210
What's <i>with</i> you? I'm here, aren't I?

13:12.200 --> 13:15.100
Yeah. That's why from now on, always...

13:15.850 --> 13:18.250
You want a promise of that far away in the future?

13:18.860 --> 13:21.690
Even if it is, I want that promise.

13:22.440 --> 13:23.200
Huh?

13:24.380 --> 13:31.340
I've got so much used to staying with you, that I'm scared to live alone.

13:32.050 --> 13:32.860
That's still...

13:33.500 --> 13:34.860
I want your promise.

13:35.800 --> 13:39.050
But I <i>am</i> here! Why are you dissatisfied?

13:40.960 --> 13:44.970
I'm not dissatisfied. Just happy that you chose me.

14:00.660 --> 14:01.560
There.

14:02.180 --> 14:05.680
Aikawa-san, I finished sorting the fan letters and presents.

14:05.900 --> 14:10.570
Thank you! It's a huge pain to sort out all the Valentine's Day chocolates every year.

14:10.700 --> 14:13.420
You've been a big help since you joined here part-time.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.720
Is there anything else to be done?

14:16.860 --> 14:19.980
Then, could you give Usami-sensei his share of chocolates?

14:20.240 --> 14:21.980
You can just take then home and call it a day.

14:22.140 --> 14:24.300
What? All of these?

14:25.200 --> 14:30.000
We can give him the letters later, so just take all the cream chocolates and perishables first.

14:31.210 --> 14:35.100
Amazing! Usagi-san is so popular.

14:35.290 --> 14:37.540
And these are all branded chocolates to boot.

14:40.180 --> 14:41.680
Oh, Isaka-san!

14:41.680 --> 14:44.620
What's up? Did Akihiko do something again?

14:44.850 --> 14:49.130
Oh, no. Starting today, I'm doing temporary part-time job for Aikawa-san.

14:49.740 --> 14:50.840
Really?

14:51.490 --> 14:54.850
Oh, yeah. Did you hear from Haruhiko after that day?

14:54.940 --> 14:56.680
Eh? Not really.

14:56.970 --> 14:58.560
Oh? I see.

14:59.380 --> 15:01.220
<i>What's he trying to say?</i>

15:01.600 --> 15:05.460
<i>As I thought, I still feel uncomfortable around Isaka-san.</i>

15:07.690 --> 15:11.420
Director, Usami-sama has arrived.

15:14.480 --> 15:15.200
Hm?

15:16.460 --> 15:17.730
<i>Usagi's father!!</i>

15:18.010 --> 15:22.200
OOh!! We really do meet each other in unexpected places, don't we, Takahashi-kun?

15:22.780 --> 15:25.860
It seems I need to thank you about Haruhiko.

15:29.620 --> 15:32.500
That's right. Why don't we go for lunch after this?

15:32.570 --> 15:37.460
What are you saying? You have a meeting after this and we'll be going for lunch together.

15:37.660 --> 15:42.120
Well, to be honest, having lunch with a bunch of old men is just...

15:42.200 --> 15:44.930
Sorry. I'm in a bit of a hurry. So please excuse me.

15:45.220 --> 15:46.420
Takahashi-kun,

15:47.460 --> 15:48.960
is Akihiko doing well?

15:49.920 --> 15:51.050
He's fine.

15:58.980 --> 16:00.040
<i>What's this? </i>

16:00.700 --> 16:03.040
<i>A lot of things happened in Atami and afterwards,</i>

16:04.200 --> 16:06.620
<i>so I always think his words have spite in them.</i>

16:12.130 --> 16:14.800
<i>Is it okay for me to buy some chocolates for Usagi-san too?</i>

16:15.540 --> 16:18.480
<i>No, but Usagi-san doesn't like sweet food.</i>

16:18.960 --> 16:23.460
<i>Uh, to begin with, a guy giving chocolates to another guy is a bit...</i>

16:29.320 --> 16:30.880
Oh, Takahashi-kun!

16:31.010 --> 16:31.780
Eh!?

16:33.260 --> 16:35.520
That's good. I waited for you.

16:35.740 --> 16:38.650
U-Uh... What about the meeting with Isaka-san?

16:38.970 --> 16:41.220
I dumped it on Haruhiko.

16:41.600 --> 16:44.620
I tried to contact on the intercom but nobody answered,

16:44.820 --> 16:47.940
Oh, Usagi-san pretends he's not home when he's busy.

16:48.020 --> 16:49.650
Wait, you're coming over?

16:49.770 --> 16:51.880
Yes. Could you let me in?

16:52.120 --> 16:55.120
Oh, but Usagi-san is currently in the middle of his work.

16:55.920 --> 16:58.620
<i>W-Wait a minute. If I do that, Usagi-san would...</i>

16:58.620 --> 17:00.620
It's okay for a little while, right?

17:00.770 --> 17:02.620
Oh, no, but still...

17:03.820 --> 17:08.620
Excuse me Takahashi-kun, but I'm Akihiko's father, you know.

17:13.740 --> 17:17.320
Misaki, you're back? I'm starving.

17:17.460 --> 17:18.500
What's for dinner tonight?

17:18.810 --> 17:20.460
Stew, apparently.

17:22.060 --> 17:24.370
With minced peas in it.

17:26.530 --> 17:28.520
Don't glare at people like that.

17:28.520 --> 17:32.060
What's the meaning of this? Would you please not come to my house as you wish?

17:32.250 --> 17:34.010
Today's Valentine's Day, right?

17:34.010 --> 17:36.400
I had some chocolates custom made, so I came to give them to you.

17:36.740 --> 17:39.120
I don't want them. Please hurry up and go back.

17:39.520 --> 17:41.860
Um, Usagi-san, I invited him over.

17:42.060 --> 17:43.060
We met just close by so-

17:43.060 --> 17:44.040
Don't lie!

17:49.330 --> 17:52.360
You're leading a much more decent life than I expected.

17:52.800 --> 17:55.080
So, what's your real motive of coming here?

17:56.020 --> 17:59.410
Is it wrong for a father to be interested in his son's life?

18:01.140 --> 18:04.520
Oh, dear. Looks like I'm hated a lot.

18:05.050 --> 18:07.940
Well, just like you said, I have a motive in coming here.

18:08.730 --> 18:09.600
What's this?

18:09.680 --> 18:11.980
Exactly what it looks like, photos of prospective brides.

18:13.900 --> 18:16.600
I was wondering what you came here for. So useless.

18:16.820 --> 18:18.860
Misaki, go to your room.

18:18.940 --> 18:20.040
But the tea?

18:20.290 --> 18:21.240
It's okay.

18:22.080 --> 18:23.320
Takahashi-kun.

18:24.530 --> 18:25.420
<i>What should I do?</i>

18:25.880 --> 18:29.690
I said this at the office also, but thank you once again for rejecting Haruhiko.

18:30.280 --> 18:32.200
<i>If I stay here like this...</i>

18:32.320 --> 18:34.640
You saying things out clearly really helped.

18:34.810 --> 18:36.240
<i>unpleasant words...</i>

18:36.330 --> 18:38.250
Misaki, just go to your room!

18:38.360 --> 18:40.090
<i>words I don't want to hear...</i>

18:40.780 --> 18:42.530
Just like this, next, could you...

18:42.740 --> 18:44.080
<i>I'll have to hear them.</i>

18:44.340 --> 18:46.520
...reject Akihiko too?

18:47.090 --> 18:49.960
Your existence is a hindrance to me.

18:55.880 --> 18:57.960
U-Uh... Usagi-san!

18:58.320 --> 19:03.940
To deny Misaki's existence is the same as denying my existence.

19:04.900 --> 19:07.900
If he's not here, I can't go on living.

19:10.100 --> 19:10.780
Let's go.

19:10.940 --> 19:12.440
What? Where?

19:12.620 --> 19:13.930
We'll eat out tonight.

19:15.600 --> 19:18.330
The door has an auto-lock, so feel free to go back whenever you wish.

19:19.970 --> 19:21.530
Oh dear.

19:23.320 --> 19:27.820
I wasn't saying that I hate Takahashi-kun or anything, you know.

19:28.130 --> 19:29.820
Please don't follow us.

19:29.820 --> 19:30.960
You're being annoying!

19:31.100 --> 19:37.940
It's not 100% true that you'll be happy if you are living with the person you love.

19:38.020 --> 19:40.880
I have no obligation to take orders from you!

19:41.600 --> 19:43.940
I'm just worried about you.

19:44.520 --> 19:48.280
If you think you're happy right now, then it's just an illusion.

19:48.620 --> 19:52.090
The one who decides if it's an illusion or not isn't you, but me!

19:52.250 --> 19:54.170
H-Hey, w-wait Usagi-san! That's dange-

19:55.900 --> 19:56.770
Usagi-san!!

20:08.580 --> 20:10.520
Akihiko!! Are you alright!!?

20:15.420 --> 20:18.800
You should cross only when the signal turns blue*! You were taught that in school, weren't you!!?

20:15.420 --> 20:18.800
*In Japanese, a green traffic light is referred to as literally "blue". The reason for this apparent mismatch is that the character used for the colour blue contains connotations of the colour green.

20:19.300 --> 20:20.120
You idiot!!

20:20.680 --> 20:22.340
Not blue, but green.

20:22.540 --> 20:23.730
Don't argue with me!

20:23.780 --> 20:26.660
And you! At least teach your kids to cross a damn crossing!

20:28.540 --> 20:31.570
O-Oh, no! Sorry! I just got carried away.

20:34.180 --> 20:35.450
I see.

20:35.890 --> 20:39.250
Takahashi-kun is able to stop Akihiko too, huh.

20:39.840 --> 20:40.860
I see.

20:41.420 --> 20:42.730
Indeed.

20:45.060 --> 20:46.540
That's why I told you, right?

20:47.770 --> 20:50.970
If he's not here, I can't go on living.

20:53.970 --> 20:56.770
Even though you'd be living all alone till now, too.

20:59.880 --> 21:01.180
After meeting Misaki,

21:01.860 --> 21:06.760
I felt happy for the first time to be with someone.

21:08.840 --> 21:10.740
Even if it's not 100%,

21:12.080 --> 21:16.120
to me, it's still the truth.

21:21.420 --> 21:22.780
Oh dear.

21:26.600 --> 21:33.210
Akihiko, don't forget, that the path you have taken is going to be a very harsh.

21:34.250 --> 21:38.180
Eventually, a time will come when you will be forced to part.

21:39.760 --> 21:44.740
But... I'll try to have faith in your words for now.

21:47.960 --> 21:49.010
Takahashi-kun.

21:49.090 --> 21:50.090
Uh, yes!

21:50.780 --> 21:55.500
I'd really love to sit down and have a chat with you about bear wood carvings.

21:55.930 --> 21:57.900
Let's go for lunch sometime.

22:03.660 --> 22:04.700
See you.

22:07.640 --> 22:09.920
<i>Uh? Does this mean...</i>

22:10.810 --> 22:16.540
<i>...that Usagi's father acknowledges me?</i>

22:15.740 --> 22:20.880
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

22:15.740 --> 22:20.880
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

22:20.040 --> 22:21.210
Let's go home.

22:21.010 --> 22:26.270
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

22:21.010 --> 22:26.270
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

22:21.520 --> 22:23.460
What? We're not eating out?

22:23.860 --> 22:28.690
I prefer the stew that you prepare. But don't put any peas in it.

22:26.620 --> 22:31.640
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

22:26.620 --> 22:31.640
You doubled all my happiness,

22:29.580 --> 22:34.450
<i>Usagi-san's hands are big and cold like always and yet so warm...</i>

22:31.640 --> 22:38.330
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

22:31.640 --> 22:38.330
and halved all my sadness.

22:35.100 --> 22:38.960
<i>Right now, I'm in such a good mood </i>

22:38.440 --> 22:43.440
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:38.440 --> 22:43.440
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:39.400 --> 22:46.610
<i>that I keep thinking that he would keep his hand there forever, just like that.</i>

22:43.840 --> 22:48.120
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:43.840 --> 22:48.120
will surely lead to you.

22:48.120 --> 22:50.880
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:48.120 --> 22:50.880
You're there up ahead of me,

22:48.640 --> 22:51.000
Oh, yeah. Usagi-san.

22:50.880 --> 22:53.740
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:50.880 --> 22:53.740
I'm there ahead of you,

22:51.170 --> 22:51.960
What?

22:52.650 --> 22:53.980
Give me your hand.

22:53.740 --> 22:59.010
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:53.740 --> 22:59.010
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:58.280 --> 22:59.520
Commoner's chocolates.

22:59.010 --> 23:04.910
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:59.010 --> 23:04.910
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:59.680 --> 23:03.060
Let me just say this too. These aren't for Valentine's Day or anything, okay?

23:03.580 --> 23:06.200
I just decided to go along with this money grubbing scheme of the chocolatiers.

23:05.500 --> 23:09.980
mou doko he mo ikanaide

23:05.500 --> 23:09.980
Hey, don't go anywhere.

23:06.300 --> 23:08.810
And if you don't like that, call them "rent-payment" chocolates.

23:09.980 --> 23:15.440
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

23:09.980 --> 23:15.440
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

23:11.850 --> 23:15.090
Why do you always do things that make me so happy?

23:15.440 --> 23:20.830
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

23:15.440 --> 23:20.830
It's casting a light at my feet.

23:17.410 --> 23:19.360
I don't know anything about that.

23:19.420 --> 23:20.520
It's no good.

23:20.830 --> 23:26.650
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

23:20.830 --> 23:26.650
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

23:22.770 --> 23:27.640
It's really just that, if you aren't there, I can't go on living.

23:27.040 --> 23:32.330
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

23:27.040 --> 23:32.330
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

23:30.180 --> 23:32.380
I love you, Misaki.

23:34.980 --> 23:44.930
